* Hiwatt DR103 100 W preamp (owner's manual drawing, issue 4, serial AB0309 onwards): V1a normal and V1b brilliant input stages
* (one shared 1k5 / 100u cathode), their volume pots feeding the two halves of V2 (plates joined, one 100k load; the normal
* half has an unbypassed 1k cathode, the brilliant half 1k with 47n), the passive Hiwatt tone stack (1000p + 220p treble, 100k lin
* middle, 470k log bass, two 47n and a 100k), the 220k master volume and V3a (100k load, 1k5 cathode). The coupling 47n to the
* phase inverter and its 100k are drawn here so the preamp's output is already AC; the inverter, the V3b DC reference and
* the presence network are in poweramp.net.
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - the input jacks: 1M to ground and nothing else (the drawing shows the grids wired straight to the jacks);
*    "Jumpered" feeds the same signal into both channels;
*  - all four valves are 12AX7 (the drawing says ECC83 for V1 to V4; the specification page lists V4 as an ECC81);
*  - the capacitor between V3a's plate and the presence pot (printed "100pF", cut by the page fold) is left out: the preamp and
*    the power amp are solved separately and at 100 pF its effect is tiny;
*  - supply: the node x is HT supply 3, 10k and 32u make the V2 rail, another 10k and 16u the V1 / V3 rail.

.nodes x nb na gin in jb jn pb pn kk cb cn wb wn p2 k2a k2b ta tb tc tw u1 m l2 mt wm p3 k3 o

* HT supply 3 (node x): driven from the power amp at run time; 410 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 410
R R10A x nb 10k
C C32U nb 0 32u
R R10B nb na 10k
C C16U na 0 16u

* The guitar behind a variable source resistance, then the jack switches.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* Jacks. SW_* are the channel selector (closed 1 ohm / open 1e12), set by the jack modes. jb / jn are the V1b / V1a grids.
R SW_BRIL in jb 1
R RLEAK_B jb 0 1M
R SW_NORM in jn 1e12
R RLEAK_N jn 0 1M

* V1: two 220k plate loads from the V1 rail, one shared 1k5 / 100u cathode.
T V1B jb pb kk 12AX7
T V1A jn pn kk 12AX7
R R220B na pb 220k
R R220N na pn 220k
R RK1 kk 0 1k5
C CK1 kk 0 100u

* Brilliant channel: 1000p coupling into the 470k log volume (V2b grid). Normal channel: 22n into its 470k log volume (V2a grid).
C C_B pb cb 1n
R VR_BT cb wb 1
R VR_BB wb 0 1
C C_N pn cn 22n
R VR_NT cn wn 1
R VR_NB wn 0 1

* V2: plates joined onto 100k, 1k cathodes (the brilliant half bypassed with 47n).
T V2A wn p2 k2a 12AX7
T V2B wb p2 k2b 12AX7
R R100P nb p2 100k
R RK2A k2a 0 1k
R RK2B k2b 0 1k
C CK2B k2b 0 47n

* Tone stack: 1000p and 220p in series to the 220k lin treble pot (its bottom is tc, 220k from their junction), 22k to the
* middle (100k lin rheostat, 1000p across it), the bass (470k log rheostat to ground) and the 100k / 47n / 47n network.
C C1000T p2 ta 1n
C C220T ta tb 220p
R R220 ta tc 220k
R VR_TT tb tw 1
R VR_TB tw tc 1
R R22A tc u1 22k
R VR_MID u1 m 1
C C1000M u1 m 1n
R VR_BASS m 0 1
R R100L p2 l2 100k
C C47A l2 m 47n
C C47B l2 0 47n

* Master volume (220k lin) behind 22k from the treble wiper, then V3a.
R R22M tw mt 22k
R VR_MT mt wm 1
R VR_MB wm 0 1
T V3A wm p3 k3 12AX7
R R100V na p3 100k
R RK3 k3 0 1k5
* Coupling 47n into the phase inverter (100k to the V3b DC reference).
C C47O p3 o 47n
R RPI o 0 100k
